Benchmark refactor status

Implemented in eqlog-bench:
- Concrete native/COW workloads and a statically dispatched paired runner.
- Independent carrier, member-predicate, mixed-predicate, mixed-signature
  function, member-function and member-marking programs.
- Ambient predicate propagation and marking over chains, sparse/dense DAGs,
  balanced merge forests and finite cyclic graphs.
- Separate one-step functionality and recursive-congruence programs.
- Existing compound jobs and grouped joins retained as opt-in stress cases.
- Configurable size grids, COW bounds via --list, and full semantic oracles
  outside the single populated close measured for each sample.
- Paired ratio intervals, per-doubling growth checks, and explicit host-local
  baseline refresh/check commands. Speedups also invalidate a baseline.
- Correctness coverage remains in eqlog-test-eval; eqlog-test-opt is unchanged.

The current host expectations cover mixed predicates, ambient-to-member
functions, and both congruence cases over 24 parameter combinations.
Check them with:

cargo bench -p eqlog-bench --bench member_mapping -- \
  --case mixed-predicate,from-ambient,congruence,recursive-congruence \
  --vertices 64,128,256 --members 4,16 --keys 4,16 --depth 8 \
  --samples 15 --baseline eqlog-bench/expectations.json \
  --check --check-scaling

Use an otherwise idle, pinned CPU for comparable measurements. Replace
--check with --update-baseline to deliberately refresh the ratios; failed
scaling checks leave the existing expectations untouched. Raw reports go
to an explicitly chosen --output path, outside the checked-in expectations.

Follow-up work:
- Investigate the ordinary-storage cost of member-to-ambient functions.
  The isolated to-ambient case exposes the current compact-eligibility limit.
- Specify finite semantics before adding member-generating cycle cases.
  Existing cycle benchmarks use ambient values and finite predicate closure.
- Add independently specified overlapping member DAG cases without naming
  functions if needed. The function-free merge forest deliberately has
  unique paths, so unioning by origin does not add unintended equations.
- Extend performance expectations to other hosts only after measuring them.
